{
  "title": "Calorie estimates: sized containers, packages, balls and blocks",
  "description": "Prod (make ingredient-prod-report, 2026-10-25): 36 unweighable prod lines name a container or package, the biggest weight group in prod; 11 are fixed just by re-parsing the stored line and many others lost the package size's unit at import (see blocked-apply-prod-burndown-fixes, D2). \
Real ones left: an envelope of ranch mix (a regression), a jar of furikake, a bag of marshmallows, a cube of curry roux. \
About 35 lines (pipeline fixtures mostly) count a container or piece the catalog can't weigh. \
Done: a bundle is a bunch (\"1 bundle scallions\" x5), a USDA portion named by alternatives (\"wedge or slice\") answers to either (\"2 wedge lemon\"), and cited pieces for \"2 stick rhubarb\" (a stalk), \"1 fillet anchovy\" and \"1 package instant ramen noodles\". \
Parser/reader cases done: metric volumes on containers (\"1 750-ml bottle red wine\"), \"1 12- ounce beer\", \"10-to-12-ounce bag\", a weight leading the item after a package (\"1 package, 9 oz. chocolate wafer cookies\"), a noted weight that runs on into the item (\"1 package (.25 ounce powdered gelatin)\"), and \"roughly 2.5 - 3 pounds\" after a comma. \
Left: \"1 five-pound leg of lamb\" x3 (spelled-out leading weight; bone-in cuts are null aliases anyway, so it stays unknown) and \"10-inch flour tortillas\" with no count (the inch size reads as the unit; there's no count to weigh). \
Cited-weight cases (done: balls of pizza dough, burrata and fresh mozzarella, cream cheese blocks, and taco seasoning, brown gravy and ranch mix packages from USDA Branded labels, an envelope or packet being the package): \"1 portion no-knead pizza dough\" x2 (a portion isn't a ball by any rule yet), \"block konnyaku\" (no label gives a block), \"1 small can baby corn\", \"1 small jar roasted red peppers\", \"1 jar furikake\" x2, \"2 container petite-creme yogurt\", sized bunches (\"1 large bunch basil\", \"2 large bunch rosemary\", \"3 large stalk rosemary\", \"2-3 bunch dried somen\"), \"6 leaf nappa cabbage\", \"1 small head napa cabbage\", loaves without a sourced loaf weight (\"1 loaf bread\", \"1 loaf unsliced white bread\"; \"6 loaf pita bread\" is done: a loaf of pita is a pita), cinnamon/cassia and kombu 2-inch pieces (cinnamon is trace; kombu needs a per-inch weight). \
SR Legacy and FNDDS (the FDC CSV archives scripts/import-catalog.py downloads) have no piece for most of these; USDA Branded labels would. \
Measure with make ingredient-catalog-audit (Unsupported quantity unit, all three corpora; logs/ingredient-catalog-failures.json once #906 lands) and, once blocked-ingredient-burndown-from-prod lands, the prod report; make pipeline should produce only data/ingredient-catalog-audit.md and fixture-category diffs. \
Server-side only (ramekin-core nutrition), so no web or iOS change. \
Split out of the retired p3-nutrition-remaining-count-units (owner, 2026-10-24: whole groups per PR, never one ingredient).",
